WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:08.000
Same result. Different execution.
x + 1/3; 1/3 + x; x + (1/6 + 1/6).
What should a comparison preserve?

00:08.000 --> 00:16.000
At x = 2/3, all three return 1.
At x = 1/2, all three return 5/6.

00:16.000 --> 00:24.000
Execution-event counts:
x + 1/3: 6; 1/3 + x: 6;
x + (1/6 + 1/6): 10.

00:24.000 --> 00:28.000
The comparison observes the exact result string.
Complete executions and separate resource ledgers
retain the differences.

00:28.000 --> 00:32.000
The first two expressions evaluate
their leaves in opposite orders.

00:32.000 --> 00:36.000
What would your application observe?
The result? Event order? Resource use?

00:36.000 --> 00:40.000
